source_proof = "Offline assertions read the actual README architecture, diagrams, directory/build/release guidance, HTTPS root RPC hosts and parsed curl JSON chain probe; bind node registrations to transaction acceptance/forwarding, WAL acknowledgement before receipt publication and committed MsgSequenceBatch coverage; parse the hosted OpenRPC contract and ledger ABI; check native bank/program entry points, executor retirement guards and literal Makefile prerequisites/recipes. These prove documented source facts, not runtime behavior."
review_only = "Go/C/Rust compilation, linked paxd execution, live endpoints, signing, BFT consensus, WAL recovery and runtime producer/transport/consumer behavior are not executed. They require owning-domain qualification and review. This doc-drift task changes no interface or persistent component; no restart-recovery or interface-mismatch runtime proof is claimed. No shell script, unit file or manifest is changed; shell examples use shlex and JSON parsing, build rules use an in-process literal parser, without a subprocess toolchain, external binary, environment variable, credential, live endpoint, native artifact or device."
baseline = "No pre-change verification was run. The explicit implementation-first order permits verify_cmd only through hf-done after hf-build, superseding the contradictory unchanged-tree clause in step 5. No baseline failures are claimed. Initial git status/diff showed only runner bookkeeping in .cgignore and spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx; both scoped files were absent and /out/run/gates.jsonl was absent. README.md already contains the owning task corrections and its inspected bytes are bound by readme_sha256."
